course: dictionary
lesson: 15979
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word uplifted can describe a feeling, a raised body part, or rocks in the ground. The words around it show you which meaning to use.
explain: «I felt uplifted by the music.» Here uplifted means happier and more hopeful, because the music made the feeling better. Test it: "I felt happier by the music" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «She stood with uplifted hands.» Here uplifted means raised up high. In church and prayer, uplifted hands can be a sign of prayer or praise.
explain: «The uplifted rocks formed the mountain.» In geography, uplifted rocks have been pushed upwards by forces inside the Earth. This meaning is about movement, not feelings.
fact: Uplifted means feeling happier, more hopeful or encouraged.
fact: Uplifted also means raised up, as in «uplifted hands» or «uplifted faces».
fact: In geography, uplifted rocks have been pushed upwards by forces in the Earth.
fact: Uplifting music or words make people feel happier and more hopeful.
fact: Uplift is the verb: to uplift someone means to lift their spirits.
exercise: «The kind words left me feeling uplifted.» What does uplifted mean here? | Pushed far away | *Happier and more hopeful | Tired and sleepy | Lost in the rain
exercise: «She waved her uplifted hands in the air.» What does uplifted mean here? | Dropped down low | Cold and wet | *Raised up high | Hidden in her pockets
exercise: «Over millions of years, the land was uplifted.» In geography, what has happened to the land? | Its rocks were covered in snow | *Its rocks were pushed upwards by forces in the Earth | Its rocks melted into the sea | Its rocks were painted over
test: «The uplifting song made the whole class smile.» What does uplifting mean? | Making a loud noise | Making a mess | Making people feel sleepy | *Making people feel happier and more hopeful
test: «The uplifted faces of the crowd turned to the sky.» What does uplifted mean here? | *Raised up | Wet from the rain | Sad and gloomy | Hidden behind umbrellas
exam: «After the good news, Maya felt uplifted all day.» What does uplifted mean here? | Lifted off the ground | *Feeling happier and more hopeful | Feeling cold | Sitting very still
